  "implementation": [
    "One controller10s absolute envelope plus a separate2s supervisor reclamation candidate window;0.1s reserved inside it for handle closure. No existing native quota or runtime setting was changed.",
    "Register a returned owned launch handle before late checks. Independently supplied identity binds fixed nonce-derived controller unit/cgroup, PID/startTicks/invocation before group termination is permitted.",
    "Unverified identity permits only the already-owned direct handle to be handled. A future native driver must enforce pidfd/cgroupfd ownership and must never reopen a kill path from child JSON.",
    "Separate receipt validation, process exit, fresh group emptiness and physical close-return facts. Late new activity invalidates prior acceptance and requests at most one still-owned termination.",
    "Private stdout64KiB/stderr4KiB,4KiB per poll,512poll bound; strict metadata and JSON bindings. Preserve both consumed streams before reporting overflow or malformed poll metadata.",
    "Initial clock failures/interruption produce reports without launching. Preserve original interruption object and separate cleanup errors; unknown termination/close operations are not retried.",
    "Actual pinned envelope/library/protocol code is exercised through a same-process memory driver; failed inner results cannot be promoted by a clean transport exit."
  ],
